  "verdict": {
    "outcome": "The piecewise `extend` equals Re of the principal-branch analytic Rogers L IDENTICALLY, not just at the six ladder points. Confirmed at generic arguments from 1.000001 to 1e6 and -1e-6 to -1e6.",
    "derivation": "x > 1: Euler inversion plus principal log(-x) = log x + i*pi, on real parts. x < 0: Landen, using 1 - x/(x-1) = 1/(1-x). Both collapse exactly; see this file's docstring for the two-line versions.",
    "where_the_work_went": "down one level, not away. The Rogers-L inversion and Landen hypotheses are now free by construction, but identifying `extend` with the analytic continuation owes Li_2 inversion and Li_2 Landen -- the same two classical facts, and Mathlib has no Li_2 at all (qou-mlbg).",
    "what_is_still_owed": "those two Li_2 identities, if the Lean object is to be called the dilogarithm. Until then `extend` is a piecewise function that provably satisfies the ladder's hypotheses -- which is what the ladder needs, and less than what the name suggests.",
    "not_a_proof": "this is numerical confirmation of a paper derivation. It is run at generic points so that a coincidence cannot pass, which is the most a probe can do.",
